       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO TID, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as up to 850 mg TID. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day. A single dose is typically no more than 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** this is twice the daily maximum. It raises the risk of severe GI effects and metformin-associated lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release)\n- **1,000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO TID with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg BID\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg TID, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
